Here's a clean and efficient solution using a Union-Find (DSU) over indices connected by shared prime factors. We factor each number using a smallest-prime-factor sieve (SPF), and union indices that share any prime. If all indices end up in one connected component, return True.

Complexity: O(n log A + A log log A) where A = max(nums) for sieve + factorization, which fits constraints.

